sentences.t:
“Ne, quaeso, ne me lacrimis neve omine tanto
prosequere in duri certamina Martis euntem,
O mater;

sentences.l:
“Do not, I beg, do not with tears or with so great an omen
see me off, as into the contests of harsh Mars I go,
O mother;

as soon as tomorrow's in the sky,
on crimson borne wheels, Dawn grows red,
let him not lead the Teucrians against the Rutulians; let the Teucrians' arms rest,
and the Rutulians;
